recently immigrated from Zimbabwe to the UK presents to the emergency department with fever, myalgia and headaches. He is suspected to have malaria. Which test is most likely to allow for accurate speciation of the malaria pathogen?","options":{"A":"Thick blood film.","B":"Thin blood film.","C":"Quantitative buffy coat analysis.","D":"Blood culture."},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The source marks Thin blood film. as the most likely diagnosis/answer for the clinical pattern described."},{"id":"q_past_150","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End module group A 23","text":"Which of the following is true regarding the Salmonella species?","options":{"A":"Rose spots appear in all patients with typhoid.","B":"They are normally present in the gut as commensals.","C":"They are anaerobic organisms.","D":"A relative bradycardia is often seen in typhoid fever."},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks A relative bradycardia is often seen in typhoid fever.. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_151","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End module group A 23","text":"A 34-year-old sewage worker presents with 3 days history of low back pain, fever, myalgia, fatigue, jaundice, subconjunctival hemorrhage and renal impairment. He has no past medical history and has not been abroad in the last 6 months. What is the most likely diagnosis?","options":{"A":"Cysticercosis.","B":"Leptospirosis.","C":"Glomerulonephritis.","D":"Hepatitis A."},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The source marks Leptospirosis. as the exception. The question is testing recognition of the statement that does not fit the expected features of the condition."},{"id":"q_past_152","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End module group A 23","text":"A 34-year-old man from Zimbabwe is admitted with abdominal pain. Abdominal X- ray reveals urinary bladder calcification. What is the most likely cause?","options":{"A":"Sarcoidosis.","B":"Leishmaniasis.","C":"Schistosoma haematobium.","D":