topic":"End module group B 23","text":"Which of the following groups of viruses is most likely to cause meningitis?","options":{"A":"Adenoviruses.","B":"Human papillomaviruses.","C":"Poxviruses.","D":"Enteroviruses."},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks Enteroviruses. as the most likely diagnosis/answer for the clinical pattern described."},{"id":"q_past_163","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End module group B 23","text":"Non-blanching petechiae and cutaneous hemorrhages may be present in meningitis caused by:","options":{"A":"Viruses.","B":"Parasites.","C":"Bacteria.","D":"Tuberculosis."},"correctOption":"C","explanation":"The source identifies Bacteria. as the causative organism or etiologic answer tested by this question."},{"id":"q_past_164","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End module group B 23","text":"Which one of the following features is least likely to occur in a patient with visceral leishmaniasis?","options":{"A":"Massive splenomegaly.","B":"Diarrhoea.","C":"Pancytopenia.","D":"Grey skin."},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The source marks Diarrhoea.. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_165","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End module group B 23","text":"The most consistent pathologic finding in leptospirosis is:","options":{"A":"Vasculitis of capillaries.","B":"Endothelial edema.","C":"Necrosis.","D":"Lymphocytic infiltration."},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"The source marks Vasculitis of capillaries.. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_166","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End module group B 23","text":"All the following statements regarding HIV infection in humans are true, EXCEPT:","options":{"A":"Monocytes and macrophages are the major reservoirs of the virus.","B":"There are mainly 3 stages of HIV infection with AIDS being the most severe stage.","C":"Possible symptoms include fever, chills, fatigue, and mouth ulcers in the early stage of infection.","D":"Medicines are available for the complete cure of chronic HIV infection."},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks Medicines are available for the complete cure of chronic HIV infection. as the exception. The question is testing recognition of the statement that does not fit the expected features of the condition."},{"id":"q_past_167","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End module group B 23","text":"Which is FALSE regarding Pneumocystis carinii pneumonia in AIDS?","options":{"A":"It is usually only seen when the CD4 count is <200.","B":"Prophylaxis should be given in all patients with CD4 count <200.","C":"Chest X-ray characteristically shows bilateral diffuse infiltrates.","D":"Once a patient has had it, they are unlikely to get it again."},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks AIDS as the exception in this aseptic-fever question."},{"id":"q_past_168","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End module group B 23","text":"A 31-year-old man is evaluated in the emergency department for a 5-day history of abdominal discomfort, vomiting, and loose stools, accompanied by progressively increasing fever. He also has a moderate headache and a rash. On physical examination, temperature is 40 ° C, blood pressure is 102/78 mmHg, pulse rate is 64/min, and respiration rate is 20/min. BMI is 26. The patient appears sick. There are blanching erythematous macules on the lower chest and upper abdominal wall. The pharynx is erythematous. The remainder of the examination reveals tender hepatosplenomegaly. His CBC shows leucopenia with lymphopenia. Liver profile shows elevated liver enzymes. Two sets of aerobic blood cultures show gram-negative bacilli. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?","options":{"A":"Brucellosis.","B":"Lassa fever.","C":"Leptospirosis.","D":"Typhoid fever."},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks Typhoid fever. as the most likely diagnosis/answer for the clinical pattern described."},{"id":"q_past_169","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End semester 23","text":"Absolute contraindications to live attenuated vaccines:","options":{"A":"Severe illness that needs hospitalization.","B":"Recent receipt of blood.","C":"HIV infection.","D":"Pregnancy."},"correctOption":"C","explanation":"The source specifies symptomatic HIV infection as a contraindication to live attenuated vaccines."},{"id":"q_past_170","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End semester 23","text":"The following are true regarding schistosoma infection except:","options":{"A":"Haematuria or bleeding per rectum may be the presentation.","B":"Diagnosis can be made by finding ova in the urine and/or stool.","C":"Can be complicated by colorectal cancer.","D":"Can lead to portal hypertension."},"correctOption":"C","explanation":"The source marks Can be complicated by colorectal cancer. as the exception. The question is testing recognition of the statement that does not fit the expected features of the condition."},{"id":"q_past_171","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End semester 23","text":"Which of the following parasites is not a cause for aseptic meningitis:","options":{"A":"Naegleria.","B":"Entamoeba histolytica.","C":"Strongyloides stercoralis.","D":"Taenia solium."},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The source marks Entamoeba histolytica. as the exception. The question is testing recognition of the statement that does not fit the expected features of the condition."},{"id":"q_past_172","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End semester 23","text":"Which of the following CSF results suggests viral meningitis:","options":{"A":"Elevated CSF neutrophil count, raised protein, and low glucose.","B":"Elevated CSF lymphocytic count, normal protein, and normal glucose.","C":"Elevated CSF lymphocytic count, raised protein, and low glucose.","D":"No CSF cell count, normal protein, and normal glucose."},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The source marks Elevated CSF lymphocytic count, normal protein, and normal glucose.. This is the key association being tested by t