"The source marks Urine culture; cephalexin as the treatment/management choice for the clinical situation described."},{"id":"q_past_360","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End Module Group B 2025","text":"What test is needed to determine the cause of a central line-associated bloodstream infection (CLABSI)?","options":{"A":"Blood cultures","B":"Complete blood count","C":"Chemistry","D":"Glucose"},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"The source identifies Blood cultures as the causative organism or etiologic answer tested by this question."},{"id":"q_past_361","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End Module Group B 2025","text":"Which laboratory test helps identify a patient with spontaneous bacterial peritonitis (SBP)?","options":{"A":"Positive blood culture","B":"Ascitic cell count and differential","C":"Ascitic albumin","D":"Serum ammonia"},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The source marks Ascitic cell count and differential. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_362","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End Module Group B 2025","text":"When TB affected bone that called:","options":{"A":"Osteomyelitis","B":"Sickle cell anaemia","C":"Diabetes mellitus","D":"Pott''s disease"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks Pott''s disease. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_363","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End Module Group B 2025","text":"The nurse must assign a room to a patient with scabies which of the following is the best option for this patient:","options":{"A":"A negative pressure room isolation","B":"Private room","C":"A semiprivate room with any patient","D":"A room with another patient of scabies"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks A room with another patient of scabies. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_364","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End Module Group B 2025","text":"A 30 years old man presents with a widespread maculopapular rash an