:"A 28 years old HIV-positive woman who is 38 weeks into her first pregnancy... What would you advise her regarding breastfeeding?","options":{"A":"She can breastfeed regardless of the viral load","B":"Breast feeding not recommended","C":"She can breastfeed as long as the baby is on the neonatal antiretroviral therapy","D":"She can breastfeed to a maximum of approximately 100 ml a day","E":"She can breastfeed as long as the viral load remains at <50 copies"},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The source marks Breast feeding not recommended. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_369","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End Module Group B 2025","text":"20-year-old has a sore throat and develops a diffuse rash after administration of ampicillin. The most appropriate infectious agent is:","options":{"A":"Herpes simplex virus","B":"Epstein-Barr virus","C":"Parvovirus B19","D":"Staphylococcus aureus"},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The source marks Epstein-Barr virus. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_370","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End Module Group B 2025","text":"Which is not an AIDS defining illness?","options":{"A":"Esophageal candidiasis","B":"Pneumocystis carinii pneumonia","C":"CD4 count <200 cells/micro L","D":"Herpes Zoster"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks AIDS as the exception in this aseptic-fever question."},{"id":"q_past_371","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End Module Group B 2025","text":"A young boy was playing with a kitten and now has cat scratch disease. Which bacteria species is the most likely cause?","options":{"A":"Brucella","B":"Campylobacter","C":"Borrelia","D":"Bartonella"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks Bartonella as the most likely diagnosis/answer for the clinical pattern described."},{"id":"q_past_372","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End Module Group B 2025","text":"What category of bioterrorism agents does the CDC characterize as easily transmitted from animal to person, have a high mortality rate, and include Anthrax, plague, and Ebola?","options":{"A":"Category A","B":"Category B","C":"Category C","D":"Category D"},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"Woolsorter ’ s disease is the inhalational form of anthrax associated with contaminated animal products."},{"id":"q_past_373","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End Module Group B 2025","text":"Which population is particularly at risk of severe complications from toxoplasmosis?","options":{"A":"Healthy adults","B":"Children under 5 years","C":"Pregnant women and immunocompromised individuals","D":"Athletes"},"correctOption":"C","explanation":"The source marks Pregnant women and immunocompromised individuals. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_374","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End Module Group B 2025","text":"The malaria complications can lead to hemolytic anemia and symptoms like jaundice, discoloration of the urine can be seen, which of the following name have been given to this type of complication?","options":{"A":"Rift valley fever","B":"Yellow fever","C":"Black water fever","D":"Kala Azar"},"correctOption":"C","explanation":"The source marks Black water fever. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_375","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End Module Group B 2025","text":"Which regimen would you recommend for the treatment of Egyptian chronic hepatitis C?","options":{"A":"Elbasvir/grazoprevir","B":"Glecaprevir/pibrentasvir","C":"Sofosbuvir/daclatasvir","D":"Sofosbuvir/simeprevir"},"correctOption":"C","explanation":"The source marks Sofosbuvir/daclatasvir as the treatment/management choice for the clinical situation described."},{"id":"q_past_376","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End Module Group B 2025","text":"How is Leptospirosis treated for humans?","options":{"A":"Doxycycline and amoxicillin","B":"Sulphamethoxazol-trimethoprim","C":"Chloroquine","D":"Ribavirin"},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"The source marks Doxycycline and amoxicillin. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_377","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End Module Group B 2025","text":"What drug is used to treat lymphatic filariasis caused by Wuchereria bancrofti except:","options":{"A":"Doxycycline","B":"Diethylcarbamazine","C":"Ivermectin","D":"Atebrine"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks Atebrine as the exception. The question is testing recognition of the statement that does not fit the expected features of the condition."},{"id":"q_past_378","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End Module Group B 2025","text":"Health care worker sustains needle stick injury from known case of HIV positive while taking Arterial Blood Gases sample, what to do after washing hands:","options":{"A":"Immediate p24 HIV test to health care worker to determine treatment","B":"Oral antiretroviral therapy for 4 week and reevaluate","C":"Oral antiretroviral therapy for 12 week and reevaluate","D":"Intravenous zidovudine"},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The source marks Oral antiretroviral therapy for 4 week and reevaluate. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_379","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End Module Group B 2025","text":"Which of the following is preferred as initial diagnostic test for H pylori:","options":{"A":"Upper endoscope and biopsy","B":"Stool antigen test","C":"Urea breath test"},"correctOption":"C","explanation":"The source marks Urea breath test. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_380","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End Module Group B 2025","text":"Which of the following forms of acute viral hepatitis has a much higher mortality in pregnant than non- pregnant females?","options":{"A":"Hepatitis A","B":"Hepatitis B","C":"Hepatitis C","E":"Hepatitis E"},"correctOption":"E","explanation":"The source marks Hepatitis E. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_381","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End Module Group B 2025","text":"Severe acute respiratory syndrome is caused by?","options":{"A":"Coronavirus","B":"Rhinovirus","C":"Herpesvirus","D":"Adenovirus"},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"The source identifies Coronavirus as the causative organism or etiologic answer tested by this question."},{"id":"q_past_382","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"Newly born child to HBV infected mother should receive which of the following:","options":{"A":"One dose of immunoglobulin and first dose of HBV Vaccine","B":"First dose of HBV vaccine alone","C":"One dose of immunoglobulin alone","D":"No need for HBV OR Immunoglobulin"},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"The source marks One dose of immunoglobulin and first dose of HBV Vaccine. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_383","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"Which of the following laboratory results is common in severe form of leptospirosis:","options":{"A":"Leukocytosis","B":"Thrombocytopenia","C":"Hyponatremia","D":"Eosinophilia"},"correctOption":"C","explanation":"The source marks Hyponatremia. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_384","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"All the following are criteria of Viral hemorrhagic fever except:","options":{"A":"Have a specific treatment","B":"Low infective dose is required","C":"May be used in bioterrorism","D":"Transmitted from human to human"},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"The source marks Have a specific treatment as the exception. The question is testing recognition of the statement that does not fit the expected features of the condition."},{"id":"q_past_385","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"The following viral hemorrhagic fever has WHO approved vaccine for travelers:","options":{"A":"Yellow fever","B":"Dengue fever","C":"Ebola virus","D":"Rift valley fever"},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"Faget sign (relative bradycardia with fever) is classically associated with yellow fever in this source."},{"id":"q_past_386","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"Within the body, TB organism:","options":{"A":"Are engulfed and killed with macrophages","B":"Are walled off by macrophages in encapsulated granulomas called tubercles","C":"Reside indefinitely in an active stage in the body","D":"Replicate and gain access to lymphatic channels through blood stream"},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The source identifies Are walled off by macrophages in encapsulated granulomas called tubercles as the causative organism or etiologic answer tested by this question."},{"id":"q_past_387","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"A patient is to begin IV antibiotic therapy for a pulmonary infection, what should be completed before the first dose of antibiotic is administered?","options":{"A":"Sputum culture","B":"Chest X-ray","C":"Red blood cell count","D":"Tuberculin test"},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"The source marks Sputum culture. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_388","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"People with Helicobacter pylori infection are 3 to 6 times more likely to develop stomach cancer. Which of the following cancers is NOT associated with H. pylori infection?","options":{"A":"Adenocarcinoma of the antrum","B":"Adenocarcinoma of the gastric body","C":"Cancer of the gastric cardia","D":"Gastric lymphoma"},"correctOption":"C","explanation":"The source marks Cancer of the gastric cardia as the exception. The question is testing recognition of the statement that does not fit the expected features of the condition."},{"id":"q_past_389","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"A 79-year-old male with a 20-year history of diabetes mellitus has recently developed dementia... which of the fungal infections is associated with this condition?","options":{"A":"Aspergillosis","B":"Candidiasis","C":"Mucormycosis","D":"Sporotrichosis"},"correctOption":"C","explanation":"The source marks Mucormycosis. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_390","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"During the asymptomatic phase the only evidence of infection with TB may be:","options":{"A":"Dry cough and fever","B":"Chest pain and dyspnea","C":"Cervical node enlargement","D":"Skin test reactivity to tuberculin test"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks Skin test reactivity to tuberculin test. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_391","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"The chain of infection has five main components. The habitat in which the agent normally lives, grows, and multiplies is known as the:","options":{"A":"The reservoir of infection","B":"The portal of exit","C":"Mode of transmission","D":"Portal of entry"},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"The source marks The reservoir of infection. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_392","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"One of the following vaccines is not given to symptomatic HIV children:","options":{"A":"HAV","B":"HBV","C":"OPV","D":"DPT","E":"None of the above"},"correctOption":"C","explanation":"The source marks OPV as the exception. The question is testing recognition of the statement that does not fit the expected features of the condition."},{"id":"q_past_393","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"The WHO established a standardized vaccination schedule for the original EPI which included the following vaccines except:","options":{"A":"Bacillus Calmette-Gu é rin (BCG)","B":"Rota virus vaccine","C":"Diphtheria-tetanus-pertussis (DTP)","D":"Oral polio, and Measles"},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The original EPI vaccine package did not include rotavirus vaccine in the schedule described by the source."},{"id":"q_past_394","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"An example of secondary prevention is:","options":{"A":"Giving iron to pregnant females","B":"Influenza vaccine for the elderly","C":"DPT immunization for infant","D":"Detection of asymptomatic cases of diabetes mellitus"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks Detection of asymptomatic cases of diabetes mellitus. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_395","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"A 6-year-old boy and his parents present with a 4-day history of oily, foul smelling diarrhea after a camping trip. Which medication is most appropriate?","options":{"A":"Clindamycin","B":"Itraconazole","C":"Levofloxacin","D":"Metronidazole"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks Metronidazole. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_396","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"Photodermatitis and phototoxicity are possible side effects of:","options":{"A":"Chloroquine","B":"Quinine","C":"Primaquine","D":"Mefloquine"},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"The source marks Chloroquine. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_397","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"A 29-year-old woman develops severe vomiting four hours after having a meal at a local restaurant. What is the most likely causative organism?","options":{"A":"Escherichia coli","B":"Shigella","C":"Salmonella","D":"Staphylococcus aureus"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks Staphylococcus aureus as the most likely diagnosis/answer for the clinical pattern described."},{"id":"q_past_398","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"A 23-year-old student returns from India and develops Plasmodium vivax malaria resistant to chloroquine. Most appropriate initial management?","options":{"A":"Primaquine","B":"Atovaquone-proguanil","C":"Quinine","D":"Artemether-lumefantrine"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks Artemether-lumefantrine as the treatment/management choice for the clinical situation described."},{"id":"q_past_399","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"An 18-year-old man is bitten by a forest dog. What is the most appropriate advice after thorough cleansing of the wound?","options":{"A":"Give human rabies immunoglobulin + full course of vaccination","B":"Give human rabies immunoglobulin + oral penicillin for the next 2 weeks","C":"Advise low risk but take oral co-amoxiclav for the dog bite","D":"Give human rabies immunoglobulin"},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"The source marks Give human rabies immunoglobulin + full course of vaccination. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_400","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"A 23-year old health care assistant sustained a needle-stick injury on Friday afternoon from a known HIV case and presents Monday morning.","options":{"A":"Do a HIV test today to see if she has contracted HIV","B":"Immediately start post-exposure prophylaxis","C":"Too late to start post-exposure prophylaxis","D":"Hepatitis B injection today"},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The source marks Immediately start post-exposure prophylaxis. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_401","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"A 22-year-old man presents with fatigue and sore throat for two weeks. Likely diagnosis is infectious mononucleosis. Which complication is he at risk from?","options":{"A":"Subacute sclerosing panencephalitis","B":"Splenic rupture","C":"Iron-deficiency anaemia","D":"Encephalitis"},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The source marks Splenic rupture as the most likely diagnosis/answer for the clinical pattern described."},{"id":"q_past_402","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"Ribavirin may be active against the following viral hemorrhagic fever virus:","options":{"A":"Yellow fever","B":"Dengue fever","C":"Ebola virus","D":"Rift valley fever"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks Rift valley fever. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_403","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"A 44-year-old farmer presents with headache, fever, myalgia, nausea, oliguria and subconjunctival hemorrhage. Most likely diagnosis?","options":{"A":"Mycoplasma pneumonia","B":"Lyme disease","C":"Legionella pneumonia","D":"Listeria","E":"Leptospirosis"},"correctOption":"E","explanation":"The source marks Leptospirosis as the most likely diagnosis/answer for the clinical pattern described."},{"id":"q_past_404","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"Steroids are of benefit in the treatment of:","options":{"A":"Visceral leishmaniasis","B":"Escherichia coli septicaemia","C":"Cerebral malaria","D":"Severe typhoid fever"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks Severe typhoid fever as the treatment/management choice for the clinical situation described."},{"id":"q_past_405","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"As regard Plasmodium falciparum which is not true:","options":{"A":"Causes more severe disease in pregnancy","B":"Is associated with recurrent relapses after initial treatment because of liver hypnozoites","C":"Is the only malarial parasite causing greater than 20% parasitaemia","D":"Infection is typically associated with thrombocytopaenia"},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"Plasmodium falciparum is the malaria species associated with the most severe disease and major complications."},{"id":"q_past_406","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"Subcutaneous nodules are a typical finding in:","options":{"A":"Hydatid disease","B":"Cerebral malaria","C":"Onchocerciasis","D":"Trichinosis"},"correctOption":"C","explanation":"Onchocerciasis due to Onchocerca volvulus is the cause of river blindness."},{"id":"q_past_407","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"Concerning plague:","options":{"A":"It is caused by Bacillus pestis","B":"The main vector is the rat","C":"The pneumonic form is more common than the bubonic form","D":"Direct person to person spread may occur"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks Direct person to person spread may occur. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_408","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"The following infectious agent cause dementia:","options":{"A":"Gonococcus","B":"HIV","C":"Brucella abortus","D":"Borrelia recurrentis"},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The source identifies HIV as the causative organism or etiologic answer tested by this question."},{"id":"q_past_409","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"Cinchonism is a possible side effect for:","options":{"A":"Chloroquine","B":"Quinine","C":"Primaquine","D":"Proguanil"},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The source marks Quinine. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_410","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"The most prevalent worldwide mosquito borne viral infection is:","options":{"A":"Yellow fever","B":"Dengue fever","C":"Ebola virus","D":"Rift valley fever"},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The travel history plus acute fever, myalgia/arthralgia, and retro-orbital headache are the classic clinical pattern of dengue in the source."},{"id":"q_past_411","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"Giving routine iron and folic acid to all pregnant women is a form of:","options":{"A":"Primary prevention","B":"Secondary prevention","C":"Tertiary prevention","D":"Chemoprophylaxis"},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"The source marks Primary prevention. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_412","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"Which of the following parasites inhabits large intestine:","options":{"A":"Ascaris lumbricoides","B":"Strongyloides stercoralis","C":"Ancylostoma duodenale","D":"Enterobius vermicularis"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks Enterobius vermicularis. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_413","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"Common symptoms of urethritis include:","options":{"A":"Dysuria","B":"Urethral discharge","C":"Frequency","D":"All of the above"},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"The source marks Dysuria. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_414","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"What is the main virulence factor of Brucella?","options":{"A":"Enterotoxin production","B":"Capsule","C":"Intracellular survival","D":"Endotoxin"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks Endotoxin. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_415","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"A 30-year-old veterinarian presents with malaise, chills, sweats, fatigue and intermittent fever. Most likely etiologic agent?","options":{"A":"Yersinia enterocolitica","B":"Yersinia pestis","C":"Rickettsia","D":"Brucella abortus"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"Brucella abortus is a major cause of brucellosis and is associated with the classic occupational/animal exposure setting."},{"id":"q_past_416","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"A 41-year-old HIV-infected male who refused ART is diagnosed with Pneumocystis jirovecii infection.","options":{"A":"Is at elevated risk for encephalitis","B":"Has a life expectancy of about 5 years","C":"Probably has declining levels of plasma viremia","D":"Probably has a CD4 T cell count below 200 cells/mm ³"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks Probably has a CD4 T cell count below 200 cells/mm ³ . This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_417","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"A 55-year-old diabetic man presents with headache, fever, photophobia, neck stiffness and a non- blanching rash. Most likely causative organism?","options":{"A":"Strongyloides stercoralis","B":"Human herpes virus","C":"Neisseria meningitidis","D":"TB"},"correctOption":"C","explanation":"Neisseria meningitidis is a classic cause of acute bacterial meningitis and meningococcal outbreaks."},{"id":"q_past_418","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"Which of the following drugs is administered as prophylaxis to close contacts of bacterial meningitis?","options":{"A":"Ampicillin","B":"Aminoglycoside","C":"Rifampicin","D":"Vancomycin"},"correctOption":"C","explanation":"The source marks Rifampicin. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_419","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"30-year-old man returned from Saudi Arabia with fever, joint pain, myalgia and retro-orbital headache. Most probable diagnosis?","options":{"A":"Malaria","B":"Chicken pox","C":"TB","D":"Dengue"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The travel history plus acute fever, myalgia/arthralgia, and retro-orbital headache are the classic clinical pattern of dengue in the source."},{"id":"q_past_420","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"A patient with nuchal rigidity and headache undergoes lumbar puncture. CSF shows markedly increased lymphocytes, high protein and low glucose. Most likely causative organism?","options":{"A":"Enteroviruses","B":"Cysticercosis","C":"Haemophilus influenzae","D":"TB"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks TB as the most likely diagnosis/answer for the clinical pattern described."},{"id":"q_past_421","source":"Past Exam","topic":"END MODULE B 2024","text":"The main causative agent of urinary tract infections is:","options":{"A":"Klebsiella pneumoniae","B":"Staphylococcus","C":"Pseudomonas aeruginosa","D":"Escherichia coli"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks Escherichia coli. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_422","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"Nephrotic syndrome is a recognized complication of one of the following:","options":{"A":"Schistosoma mansoni","B":"Schistosoma hematobium","C":"Plasmodium falciparum","D":"Hepatitis A virus","E":"Plasmodium thing"},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"The source marks Schistosoma mansoni. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_423","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"One of The following is not recognized cause of eosinophilia","options":{"A":"visceral larva migrans (toxocariasis)","B":"visceral leishmaniasis","C":"billharziasis","D":"drug hypersensitivity"},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The source marks visceral leishmaniasis as the exception. The question is testing recognition of the statement that does not fit the expected features of the condition."},{"id":"q_past_424","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"Mosquitoes are the vector in the following disorders","options":{"A":"onchocerciasis","B":"visceral leishmaniasis","C":"mylasis","D":"African trypanosomiasis","E":"Bancroftian filariasis"},"correctOption":"E","explanation":"The source marks Bancroftian filariasis. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_425","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"A young woman undergoes upper endoscopy for unexplained nausea, and vomiting, the stomach appears normal. Surveillance gastric biopsies are taken and the gastric biopsies ureate test is positive. The biopsies are most likely to show:","options":{"A":"Helicobacter pylori organism, but no gastric or esophageal inflammation","B":"Helicobacter pylori organism plus gastric inflammation (gastritis)","C":"Helicobacter pylori organisms plus esophagitis","D":"Neither Helicobacter pylori organisms, nor inflammation because the ureate test is often false positive with a normal endoscopy"},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The source marks Helicobacter pylori organism plus gastric inflammation (gastritis) as the most likely diagnosis/answer for the clinical pattern described."},{"id":"q_past_426","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"A diabetic patient is admitted with elevated sugar and acidosis, the patient complaining of heartache and sinus tenderness and has black necrotic material draining from nares the most likely causative organism is:","options":{"A":"Mucormycosis","B":"Histoplasmosis","C":"Candidiasis","D":"Coccidioidomycosis"},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"The source marks Mucormycosis as the most likely diagnosis/answer for the clinical pattern described."},{"id":"q_past_427","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"43-years Egyptian engineer complaining of hematuria, cystoscopy revealing squamous cell carcinoma of urinary bladder what is the etiology:","options":{"A":"E Coli","B":"salmonella typhi","C":"Schistosoma hematobium","D":"Schistosoma mansoni"},"correctOption":"C","explanation":"The source marks Schistosoma hematobium. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_428","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"21-Years old student coming from trip to Brazil with non-healing ulcer on his face the diagnosis of Leishmania braziliensis is confirmed by biopsy what is the most appropriate treatment:","options":{"A":"Cryotherapy","B":"Intralesional stibogluconate","C":"Liposomal amphotericin B","D":"No treatment is required","E":"Paromomycin"},"correctOption":"C","explanation":"The source marks Liposomal amphotericin B. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_429","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"A 47-Years old man known to be HIV coming with wide spread papules, biopsy of one of them Human Herpes Virus 8 (HHV8) is positive what the etiology is:","options":{"A":"Bacillary Angiomatosis","B":"Kaposi sarcoma","C":"Stevens-Johnson syndrome","D":"Sporotrichosis","E":"Malignant melanoma"},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The source marks Kaposi sarcoma. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_430","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"A Nurse administer an intramuscular injection to an HIV positive women after the injection she pricks her finger on the needle, what is the appropriate risk for acquiring HIV following the occupational exposure:","options":{"A":"0.003","B":"0.03","C":"0.3","D":"3%","E":"30%"},"correctOption":"C","explanation":"The source marks 0.3. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_431","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"A 44-Year old women with HIV positive CD4 count 73 presents with progressive left side hemiplegia and headache over a week MRI brain showing multiple ring-enhancing mass lesions with surrounding cerebral edema the most likely diagnosis is:","options":{"A":"brain abscess","B":"Cerebral toxoplasmosis","C":"Primary CNS lymphoma","D":"Tuberculoma","E":"Cryptococcoma"},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The source marks Cerebral toxoplasmosis as the most likely diagnosis/answer for the clinical pattern described."},{"id":"q_past_432","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"Which of the following is a contraindication to receive live rubella vaccine:","options":{"A":"Children between 1 year and puberty","B":"all exposed persons","C":"All adults","D":"Pregnant women"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks Pregnant women. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_433","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"18-year-old woman has eaten homemade food. 18 hours later, she develops ataxia, diarrhea, and dysphagia. On examination, she has tachycardia, and abnormal extra ocular movement. Cervical nerve palsy, difficulty swallowing, and change in bowel habit is the most common symptom.","options":{"A":"Clostridium botulinum toxin","B":"Staphylococcal toxin","C":"Salmonellosis","D":"Brucellosis","E":"Shigellosis"},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"Ocular toxoplasmosis can result from reactivation of congenital infection later in life."},{"id":"q_past_434","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"A 22-year-old student complains of fatigue and malaise for the past two weeks. She also reports being feverish and recently had sore throat. On examination, she has enlarged tonsils and lymphadenopathy. There is also mild tenderness in the right upper quadrant and palpable spleen. The monospot test is positive. The appropriate initial treatment is:","options":{"A":"Intravenous immunoglobulin","B":"Adequate rest and supportive treatment","C":"Ciprofloxacin","D":"Monfluradn","E":"Ampicillin"},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The source marks Adequate rest and supportive treatment as the treatment/management choice for the clinical situation described."},{"id":"q_past_435","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"A 20-year-old man develops fever, neck stiffness, and headache. Upon examination, his blood pressure is normal, his tachycardia is normal, and his feverish neck flexion is painful. No neurological symptoms are present. Which of the following is the most likely causative organism?","options":{"A":"Neisseria meningitidis","B":"Streptococcus pneumoniae","C":"Haemophilus influenzae","D":"Staphylococcus","E":"Listeria monocytogenes"},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"Neisseria meningitidis is a classic cause of acute bacterial meningitis and meningococcal outbreaks."},{"id":"q_past_436","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"What is the most likely commonest source for humans to acquire H. pylori infection?","options":