 from fundus examination, which reveals bilateral blurring of optic disc margins and retinal venous engorgement. What should be the next step?","options":{"A":"CT scan","B":"MRI brain","C":"Lumbar puncture","D":"Empiric antibiotic therapy"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks Empiric antibiotic therapy. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_441","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"Which of the following is most unlikely to be found in Clostridium difficile infection:","options":{"A":"Bloody diarrhea","B":"Fever","C":"Mild disease","D":"Leukocytosis","E":"Recurrence after therapy"},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"The source marks Bloody diarrhea. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_442","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"A patient with a previous history of tuberculosis now complaining of hemoptysis. Chest x-ray reveals upper lobe mass with a cavity and crescent-shaped air-fluid level. What is the etiology?","options":{"A":"Aspergillus flavus","B":"Coccidioidomycosis","C":"Human Parvovirus","D":"CMV"},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"The source marks Aspergillus flavus. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_443","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"A 20-year-old female sexually active with a 2-day history of dysuria, lower abdominal pain, and grade fever. Her urine is cloudy with pyuria and abundant Gram- positive bacteria are present. The organism is most likely to cause these symptoms:","options":{"A":"Enterococcus faecalis","B":"Escherichia coli","C":"Neisseria gonorrhoeae","D":"Candida albicans","E":"Staphylococcus saprophyticus"},"correctOption":"E","explanation":"The source marks Staphylococcus saprophyticus as the most likely diagnosis/answer for the clinical pattern described."},{"id":"q_past_444","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"As regard Yellow fever which is true:","options":{"A":"has a case fatality rate of 50%","B":"is caused by a flavivirus","C":"is spread by anopheline mosquitoes","D":"epidemics should be controlled by strict isolation of cases"},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"Faget sign (relative bradycardia with fever) is classically associated with yellow fever in this source."},{"id":"q_past_445","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"A 50-Years old develop sudden onset of bizarre behavior, CSF shows lymphocytes MRI show temporal lobe abnormality, what is the etiology:","options":{"A":"Epstein Barr Virus","B":"Herpes simplex virus","C":"Coxsackie virus B","D":"Neisseria gonorrhea"},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The source marks Herpes simplex virus. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_446","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"One of The following neoplasms doesn''t have a known infective etiology:","options":{"A":"Burkitt''s lymphoma","B":"Squamous carcinoma of the penis","C":"Hepatocellular carcinoma","D":"Squamous carcinoma of the bronchus","E":"Nasopharyngeal carcinoma"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks Squamous carcinoma of the bronchus. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_447","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"Adequate treatment of a case is considered as:","options":{"A":"Primary prevention for case and contact","B":"Primary prevention for case and secondary for contact","C":"Primary prevention for contact","D":"Secondary prevention of case","E":"Secondary prevention for case and primary for contact"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks Secondary prevention of case as the treatment/management choice for the clinical situation described."},{"id":"q_past_448","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"Which of the following vaccine can be given to immunocompromized patients safely?","options":{"A":"Varicella","B":"Zoster vaccine","C":"Measles","D":"HBV vaccine"},"correctOption":"D","explanation":"The source marks HBV vaccine. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_449","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"Which of the following are the reservoirs of the flea-borne typhus also called murine typhus?","options":{"A":"Rats","B":"Dogs","C":"Ticks","D":"Mites"},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"The source marks Rats. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_450","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"A nurse is teaching a new nursing assistant about ways to prevent the spread of infection, included in the instruction would be that the cycle of the infectious process must be broken, which may be:","options":{"A":"Hand washing before and between providing client care","B":"Thoroughly cleaning the environment","C":"Wearing infection control-approved protective equipment when providing patient care","D":"Using medical and surgical aseptic techniques at all times","E":"All of the above"},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"The source marks Hand washing before and between providing client care. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_451","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"An Anti-Malarial drug that is a Gametocidal and prevents transmission:","options":{"A":"Chloroquine","B":"Quinine","C":"Primaquine","D":"Mefloquine"},"correctOption":"C","explanation":"The source marks Primaquine. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_452","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"A 35-years old HIV positive CD4 count is 17 with diarrhea, tenesmus four weeks duration, blood and mucous are present in stool which of the following is the most likely diagnosis:","options":{"A":"Cryptosporidiasis","B":"Cystoisosporiasis","C":"CMV colitis","D":"Giardiasis","E":"Microsporidiosis"},"correctOption":"C","explanation":"The source marks CMV colitis as the most likely diagnosis/answer for the clinical pattern described."},{"id":"q_past_453","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"A 20 year old man who presented with persistent diarrhea and abdominal bloating after returning from a gap year in Africa is diagnosed as having strongyloidiasis. How the Strongyloides stercoralis organism would initially entered his body?","options":{"A":"Fecal-oral route","B":"Penetrated the skin","C":"Respiratory droplet route","D":"Mosquito vector"},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The source identifies Penetrated the skin as the causative organism or etiologic answer tested by this question."},{"id":"q_past_454","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"A 20-years old male presented with fever for 10 days and abdominal pain and constipation since last two days the fever chart shows step ladder pattern of fever on examination mild hepatomegaly which of the following is the most likely diagnosis:","options":{"A":"Typhoid fever","B":"Amoebiasis","C":"Tuberculosis","D":"Dengue fever"},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"The source marks Typhoid fever as the most likely diagnosis/answer for the clinical pattern described."},{"id":"q_past_455","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"Drug of choice of complicated malaria during pregnancy is:","options":{"A":"Mefloquine","B":"Primaquine","C":"Artesunate","D":"Quinine"},"correctOption":"C","explanation":"The source marks Artesunate as the treatment/management choice for the clinical situation described."},{"id":"q_past_456","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"Patient with intermittent fever presents with features treated successfully with doxycycline and rifampicin, probable diagnosis is:","options":{"A":"Brucellosis","B":"Francisella tularensis","C":"Bordetella pertussis","D":"Mycoplasma"},"correctOption":"A","explanation":"The source marks Brucellosis as the most likely diagnosis/answer for the clinical pattern described."},{"id":"q_past_457","source":"Past Exam","topi