:"Diphtheria","D":"Haemophilus influenzae"},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The source marks Parvovirus B19. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_461","source":"Past Exam","topic":"FINAL 2024","text":"A 30-Years old pregnant women develop sepsis with headache and neck stiffness after eating coleslaw, soft cheese and cantaloupes at potluck dinner, two another women who attended the event self- limiting abdominal cramps, nausea and vomiting. The causative organism is:","options":{"A":"Enterococcus faecalis","B":"Listeria monocytogenes","C":"Herpes simplex virus","D":"Staph saprophyticus"},"correctOption":"B","explanation":"The source identifies Listeria monocytogenes as the causative organism or etiologic answer tested by this question."},{"id":"q_past_462","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End module group B 26","text":"Microfilariae of Wuchereria bancrofti show:","options":{"A":"No periodicity","B":"Diurnal periodicity","C":"Nocturnal periodicity","D":"Seasonal periodicity"},"correctOption":"C","explanation":"The source marks . Nocturnal periodicity. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_463","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End module group B 26","text":"Non-gonococcal urethritis can be treated by:","options":{"A":"Single dose of azithromycin 500mg once daily for 5 days","B":"Single dose of azithromycin 500mg once daily for 5 days plus metronidazole 2gm daily for 7 days","C":"7-days course of doxycycline 100 mg orally twice daily plus metronidazole 2gm daily","D":"7-days course of doxycycline 100 mg orally twice daily"},"correctOption":"C","explanation":"The source marks 7-days course of doxycycline 100 mg orally twice daily plus metronidazole 2gm daily. This is the key association being tested by the question."},{"id":"q_past_464","source":"Past Exam","topic":"End module group B 26","text":"Which carrier is primarily in the chronic carrier state of salmonellosis:","options":{"A":"Liver","B":"Gall